IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mva-dates`
IMPORT `mva-core`
IMPORT `mva-seat`

-- Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (SA), Part 4 -- cases for the claimant's seat (mva-seat.l4). Every expected value was worked
-- by hand from the deposited text (the section is named on each group), never copied from the encoding's output. Edges:
-- the last day and the day after of each period (30 days of grace, 6 months, 21 days, 1 July 2013), month ends and leap
-- years, the $25 000 and $100 000 costs lines, age 15 and 16.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases: the claimant`

`a road car` MEANS `any other motor vehicle`
`a farm machine` MEANS `a conditionally registered tractor, agricultural machine, mobile fork lift or self-propelled lawn care machine`
`driving` MEANS `as a direct consequence of the driving of the vehicle`
`out of control` MEANS `as a direct consequence of the vehicle running out of control`
`stationary collision` MEANS `as a direct consequence of a person travelling on a road colliding with the vehicle while it was stationary, or acting to avoid such a collision`
`other way` MEANS `in some other way`
`SA policy` MEANS `insured under a CTP policy under this Part`
`the insurer answers` MEANS `the vehicle's CTP insurer: the claim is made against the insured owner or driver, and the insurer deals with it (ss 104, 125, 126A)`

§§ `s 99(3), (3a), (4)`

#ASSERT `Does my injury count as caused by the use of a motor vehicle` `driving` FALSE `a road car` TRUE EQUALS `yes: it is caused by or arises out of the use of a motor vehicle (s 99(3))`
#ASSERT `Does my injury count as caused by the use of a motor vehicle` `out of control` FALSE `a road car` FALSE EQUALS `yes: it is caused by or arises out of the use of a motor vehicle (s 99(3))`
#ASSERT `Does my injury count as caused by the use of a motor vehicle` `stationary collision` FALSE `a road car` TRUE EQUALS `yes: it is caused by or arises out of the use of a motor vehicle (s 99(3))`
#ASSERT `Does my injury count as caused by the use of a motor vehicle` `other way` FALSE `a road car` TRUE EQUALS `no: not a direct consequence of driving, running out of control, or a collision with the stationary vehicle (s 99(3))`
#ASSERT `Does my injury count as caused by the use of a motor vehicle` `out of control` TRUE `a road car` TRUE EQUALS `no: caused by a terrorist act (s 99(3a))`
#ASSERT `Does my injury count as caused by the use of a motor vehicle` `driving` FALSE `a farm machine` FALSE EQUALS `no: a conditionally registered machine that was not on a road (s 99(4))`
#ASSERT `Does my injury count as caused by the use of a motor vehicle` `driving` FALSE `a farm machine` TRUE EQUALS `yes: it is caused by or arises out of the use of a motor vehicle (s 99(3))`

§§ `s 99A(8), (10): registration 1 July 2024 to 30 June 2025; grace to 30 July 2025`

`registered` MEANS `registration (including trade plates)`

