§§ `s 126A(4), (6)(b), reg 4(3); ss 115(4), 116(5)`

#ASSERT `May I start court proceedings` TRUE EQUALS `yes: section 126A does not stop the proceedings, because the s 126A(2)(c) and (d) material has been provided (s 126A(6)(b), reg 4(3))`
#ASSERT `May I start court proceedings` FALSE EQUALS `not yet: not until the s 126A(2)(c) and (d) material is provided (s 126A(6)(b))`
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer send me a copy` (`the date` 1 3 2025) EQUALS `the date` 22 3 2025
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer send me a copy` (`the date` 20 12 2024) EQUALS `the date` 10 1 2025
#ASSERT `Could my action against the nominal defendant be dismissed for late notice` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the action cannot be dismissed on this ground: the notice was given as soon as reasonably practicable`
#ASSERT `Could my action against the nominal defendant be dismissed for late notice` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the court may dismiss the action, if the justice of the case so requires (s 115(4), s 116(5))`
#ASSERT `Could my action against the nominal defendant be dismissed for late notice` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the action cannot be dismissed on this ground: the court is not satisfied the nominal defendant was prejudiced`
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 126A(4) -- the insurer or nominal defendant must send the claimant a copy of each record it obtains within 21 days` `the insurer`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `send the claimant a copy of the record or information` 21)) EQUALS FULFILLED

§§ `ss 112, 113, 113A, 114, 124AC`

#ASSERT `Can I recover from the insurer directly` `I have a judgment against the insured person that has not been paid` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may recover from the insurer the unpaid part of the judgment that relates to the death or bodily injury, with costs or a proportionate part of them (s 112)`
#ASSERT `Can I recover from the insurer directly` `I have a judgment against the insured person that has not been paid` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 112 needs the insurer to have known of the action before it came on for hearing`
#ASSERT `Can I recover from the insurer directly` `the insured person who is liable is dead or cannot be served with process` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: you may recover by action against the insurer the amount of the judgment you could have obtained against the insured person (s 113)`
#ASSERT `Can I recover from the insurer directly` `the insured person who is liable is dead or cannot be served with process` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 113 needs your notice and short statement of grounds given as soon as possible, or in time to prevent prejudice to the insurer`
#ASSERT `Can I recover from the insurer directly` `neither` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Act gives no direct action against the insurer in this situation: the claim is made against the insured person, which the insurer conducts (s 125)`
#ASSERT `Can the insurer refuse on this ground` `the policy was obtained by mis-statement or non-disclosure` EQUALS `not a defence to an action under s 112 or s 113 (s 114)`
#ASSERT `Can the insurer refuse on this ground` `the insured person broke a term, condition or warranty of the policy or a provision of Part 4` EQUALS `not a defence to an action under s 112 or s 113 (s 114)`
#ASSERT `Can the insurer refuse on this ground` `some other ground` EQUALS `s 114 does not deal with this ground`
#ASSERT `Will the insurer pay this kind of damages` `compensatory damages for the death or bodily injury` EQUALS `the CTP insurer covers the insured person's liability for it (s 104(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Will the insurer pay this kind of damages` `aggravated damages` EQUALS `no: the CTP insurer is not liable to pay aggravated, exemplary or punitive damages; they fall on the person who was ordered to pay them (s 113A)`
#ASSERT `Will the insurer pay this kind of damages` `exemplary or punitive damages` EQUALS `no: the CTP insurer is not liable to pay aggravated, exemplary or punitive damages; they fall on the person who was ordered to pay them (s 113A)`
#ASSERT `How much are my damages after the expenses paid` 100000 5000 EQUALS 95000
#ASSERT `How much are my damages after the expenses paid` 3000 5000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much are my damages after the expenses paid` 5000 5000 EQUALS 0

